# `_ = ob_new()` begins a life the program can never end, and the runtime is
# told so: owed at exit. Until the landing review (2026-09-24) the discarded
# result was a comment in the C, nothing was owed, and the leak was exit 0.
extern "fixedbugs-a-discarded-acquisition-is-owed-at-exit.h"
    record Ob tag ob
    function ob_new() -> Ob acquires ob_put
    function ob_put(o: Ob consumes)

function main()
    _ = ob_new()
    print("acquired and dropped")
